53	Thomson	The Thomson TO and MO lines of computers were designed and manufactured in France by Thomson, between 1982 and 1986. They were mainly sold to French schools bundled with a set of not-so-great edutainment games, leading to a poor reputation for the machines. Meanwhile, the Amstrad CPC, which was cheaper, took over the home computer market. Thomson attempted to export their computers to Italia (under the Olivetti brand), Germany, and North Africa, with limited success.\r\n\r\nThe demoscene will stay away from this computer until 1988, when the Craca Cracking Company released the first prod for the Thomson TO8. There was a very small number of productions released during the 1990s, until the PULS group formed and finally managed to raise some interest on the machine.\r\n\r\nSpecs:\r\n1MHz 6809\r\nBetween 8 and 512K of RAM, depending on models\r\n8 (TO7), 16 (1st gen) or 4096 (2nd gen) colors\r\n320x200, 16 colors with block constraints (8x1 blocks) on all models\r\nExtra modes on the second generation machines:\r\n160x200, 16 colors\r\n320x200, 4 colors\r\n640x200, 2 colors\r\n\r\nThe Thomson Demoscene Page: http://exo.chez.com/indexe.html\r\n\r\nThanks to <a href="http://demozoo.org/sceners/12163/">PulkoMandy</a> for the description and image.	platform_photos/original/5/0/b6e1920db346d3b94caa108f19d3ac.jpg	500	215	platform_photos/thumb/2/a/2c9e976c9d40d1b950aa17a8ff78ee.jpg	135	89	https://media.demozoo.org/platform_photos/original/5/0/b6e1920db346d3b94caa108f19d3ac.jpg	https://media.demozoo.org/platform_photos/thumb/2/a/2c9e976c9d40d1b950aa17a8ff78ee.jpg
