39	Nintendo 64 (N64)	## Nintendo64 specific emulators\r\n\r\n[Gopher64](https://github.com/gopher64/gopher64) for Windows, Linux and macOS. Active as of May 2026.\r\n[Mupen64Plus](https://github.com/mupen64plus) for Windows, Linux and macOS. Active as of May 2026, but no releases since 2024.\r\n[Project64](https://github.com/project64/project64) for Windows. Active as of May 2026.\r\n[Rosalie's Mupen GUI](https://github.com/Rosalie241/RMG) for Windows and Linux. Active as of May 2026.\r\n[Simple64](https://github.com/simple64/simple64) for Windows, Linux and macOS. Ended development in favour of Gopher64.\r\n\r\n## Multi-system emulators\r\n\r\n[Ares](https://ares-emu.net) for Windows, Linux and macOS. Multi-format. Active as of May 2026.\r\n[BizHawk](https://github.com/TASEmulators/BizHawk) for Windows, Linux and macOS. Active as of May 2026.		\N	\N		\N	\N		
28	Sony Playstation 2 (PS2)	Demozoo has an article on how to preserve PS2 cracktros - [read here](https://demozoo.org/pages/preserving-ps2/)\r\n\r\nEmulators for this system include;\r\n\r\n[PCSX2](https://pcsx2.net/) ([github](https://github.com/PCSX2/pcsx2)) for Windows, Mac and Linux.\r\n[Play!](https://purei.org/) by Jean-Philip Desjardins  for Windows.\r\n\r\nThe first cracktro with music for this platform was [Police 24/7 (Multi) PAL/NTSC Selector](/productions/395780/) in April 2002.		\N	\N		\N	\N		
